I left out the two additions from operations. This node's declared capabilities are only `LLMClient<inference>`, so it has no import for writing files or making HTTP requests. Adding either would mean changing the node's capability set, which the graph does not grant. The HTTP call would also send raw customer text to an external service, outside the trust boundary. If operations needs logging or enrichment, it should be a separate node with its own declared capability (for example `HTTPClient` scoped to the metadata host), or logging should go through a host-side mechanism.

